.Dd November 23, 2026
.Dt HMARKET 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm hmarket
.Nd filter a saved Hetzner server-auction snapshot
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm hmarket
.Op Fl v
.Op Fl c Ar disks
.Op Fl e Ar 0|1
.Op Fl m Ar gigabytes
.Op Fl p Ar euros
.Op Fl s Ar gigabytes
.Op Fl D Ar ids
.Op Fl o Ar key=value Ns Op \&; Ns Ar key=value ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
reads one local
.Pa data/N.json.xz
snapshot of the public server-auction feed and prints
the servers that pass the filters.
It does not call Robot and it does not download the feed.
.Xr update_data 1
stores the next snapshot.
.Pp
Run it from the repository directory so
.Pa data/
resolves, or pass
.Fl o Cm jsonfile= Ns Ar path .
The file used is the highest
.Pa data/N.json.xz
whose index is still consecutive from 0.
The first missing index stops the search.
.Pp
Two filters are always on unless noted.
The disk text must contain
.Ql Enterprise HDD .
ECC is required unless
.Fl e Cm 0
is set.
.Pp
Price per TB in this table is the auction price divided
by the disk total in decimal terabytes
.Pq gigabytes divided by 1000 ,
printed with three digits after the decimal.
.Xr hcli 1
.Fl p Cm market
uses tebibytes
.Pq divided by 1024
and five digits, and it reads Robot rather than these snapshots.
.Pp
The columns are server id, RAM in gigabytes, total disk
gigabytes, disk count, price, price per TB, and the time
until the next price drop.
A past stamp on a server whose price is still moving prints
.Ql reload .
A past stamp on a fixed-price server prints
.Ql fixed .
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width "Fl o Ar key=value"
.It Fl c Ar disks
Keep servers with at least this many parsed disks.
.It Fl e Ar 0|1
ECC floor.
The default is 1, which drops non-ECC servers.
.Cm 0
keeps non-ECC servers as well.
.It Fl m Ar gigabytes
Keep servers with at least this much RAM.
.It Fl p Ar euros
Keep servers whose auction price is at most this many euros.
.It Fl s Ar gigabytes
Keep servers whose parsed disk total is at least this many gigabytes.
A
.Ql TB
size in the snapshot is multiplied by 1000.
A
.Ql GB
size is used as printed.
A disk line that matches neither form is printed with
.Ql !match
and is not counted.
.It Fl v
Print the datacenter, CPU, RAM description, and NIC lines
under each kept server.
Also print which snapshot was opened.
With
.Fl D ,
or with
.Fl o Cm id= ,
dump those server records.
.It Fl D Ar ids
Comma-separated server ids to dump when
.Fl v
is set.
.It Fl o Ar key=value
Semicolon-separated options.
.Bl -tag -width "jsonfile" -compact
.It Cm jsonfile
Read this snapshot instead of
.Pa data/N.json.xz .
.It Cm fixed
.Cm fixed=1
keeps only servers whose auction price has stopped falling.
.It Cm id
Comma-separated server ids.
Other servers are skipped.
.El
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Pa
.It Pa data/N.json.xz
Consecutive auction snapshots, starting at
.Pa data/0.json.xz .
The files are gitignored.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std hmarket
A missing snapshot exits non-zero and the message names
the path.
.Sh EXAMPLES
ECC Enterprise servers in the newest consecutive snapshot:
.Pp
.Dl ./hmarket
.Pp
One saved file, two ids:
.Pp
.Dl ./hmarket -o id=1001,1005;jsonfile=data/0.json.xz
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr hcli 1 ,
.Xr hmktst 1 ,
.Xr hmktvm 1 ,
.Xr hmktvm-picky 1 ,
.Xr update_data 1
